<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="LaunchLegit privacy policy template for legal review." noindex>
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container reveal"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</div><span class="section-kicker">Privacy</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lead">Template for review by LaunchLegit's legal counsel before publication.</p></div></section>
<section><div class="container article">
<div class="callout"><strong>Template notice:</strong> This page is intentionally a professional draft. It is not final legal advice or a binding privacy policy until reviewed, completed and approved by LaunchLegit's legal counsel.</div>
<h2>1. Information we may collect</h2><p>Depending on how the production site is configured, LaunchLegit may collect information submitted through contact or booking forms, such as name, email address, company or brand information, country and message content. Technical information such as browser type, device information and basic usage data may also be collected where analytics or security tools are enabled.</p>
<h2>2. How information may be used</h2><p>Information may be used to respond to enquiries, schedule calls, provide requested services, operate and secure the website, communicate about services and comply with applicable legal obligations. The final policy should specify the lawful bases relied upon for each processing purpose.</p>
<h2>3. Cookies and analytics</h2><p>The production website may use essential cookies and, if enabled, analytics or marketing technologies. The final version should identify each provider, cookie category, retention period and consent mechanism actually used.</p>
<h2>4. Third-party services</h2><p>Potential third parties may include scheduling, analytics, CRM, hosting, email and social platforms. The final policy should list the providers actually connected to the live website and explain relevant data transfers and processor relationships.</p>
<h2>5. GDPR and international users</h2><p>For users in the EU, EEA or UK, the final policy should explain applicable data-subject rights, lawful bases, international transfer safeguards, retention, complaint routes and how to exercise access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection and portability rights where applicable.</p>
<h2>6. Data retention and security</h2><p>LaunchLegit should define retention periods appropriate to each data category and describe proportionate technical and organizational safeguards. No website can guarantee absolute security.</p>
<h2>7. Data requests</h2><p>For privacy requests, use the contact details published on the final production website. A designated privacy contact or DPO, if applicable, should be identified here after legal review.</p>
<h2>8. Updates</h2><p>This template should be updated when processing activities, vendors, legal requirements or website functionality change.</p>
<div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Contact LaunchLegit</a></div>
</div></section>
</Layout>
